    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it's not a \"transition\" though. i don't feel like i'm changing into anything else. it's more like the light just went out. the part of me that mattered, the part that had a purpose... he's just gone. i'm just walking around in his clothes. it feels empty. like there's nothing left to actually do.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That emptiness you feel isn't just a phase; it's the void left by a core part of your identity. When the purpose evaporates, the whole structure of your daily life can feel meaningless. Instead of trying to force yourself to \"transition,\" perhaps you could focus on finding a small, tangible way to *reintroduce* something, even something tiny, into the quiet. It doesn't have to be a grand replacement for the old fire, just a flicker to see if it can catch.",
      "source": "target",
